# The `files` array in package.json is the authoritative allowlist for what gets
# published; this file changes nothing while that array is present. It is kept as
# a fallback so removing `files` would not silently start publishing the repo,
# and it is kept in step with `files` so the two never disagree.
#
# The published package is the library only: lib/, the entry points, the type
# declarations, and the four documents npm surfaces. The guide, the examples and
# the benchmarks live in the repository and on the docs site, so they are not
# installed into every consumer's node_modules.

# Tests and fixtures
test/

# Documentation site, examples and benchmarks — repository only
docs/
example/
benchmark/

# Repository and tooling
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.npmignore
.claude/
.baseline/

# Working notes, not shipped
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
TASK_PROGRESS.md

# Build and release artefacts
RELEASE_NOTES.md
*.tgz
*.log
.DS_Store

# Development-only tooling. `files` lists typescript/*.d.ts, so the compiler
# config and the type-check fixture beside them are not part of the package.
scripts/
typescript/example.ts
typescript/tsconfig.json
